A||||3||Orlando||Rattling Door
Z||000000||Orlando||07-18-99||09:40 AM||||OK, you guys have helped me to solve one of my niggling problems, here's another one:<p>The drivers door on my '88 Formula rattles whenever I hit a bump in the road. I've heard some comments about replacing the door pins. I can get the GM replacement pins at my local auto parts store. Is this a common thing, or should I take the car to a body shop so the door can be realinged? By the way, as far as I know the car has not been in any accidents, and it tracks perfectly straight and true.<p>Respond here or by email - ocabrera2@msn.com<p>Thanks again.
Z||000001||batboy||07-18-99||10:15 AM||||Yes, wear on the door hinge pins along with wear on the latch and striker pin all conspire to cause the door to rattle. With the door of my 87 half open, if I pull up and down on the door, I see movement in the hinge pin and bushing area. I temporarily quieted some of the rattles by adjusting the striker pin in a bit. If you loosen up the striker pin with a torque bit socket, you can adjust it. I've gotten in a habit of regularly greasing the door hinges and latch.
Z||000002||lowCG||07-19-99||12:29 AM||||Just put a pair of little bronze bushings into my upper hinge;pulled the upper pin out,with the door supported,let it down just to where I could get the bushings out,then in with new ones,door up,pin back into place.<br>Bushings cost me $1.26 including tax,at an Oldsmobile dealer,figured they'd all be the same.Think they have oversize bushings for cars(taxicabs)whose hinges' bores have become oval from use also.<br>I just got this car that'd never had the door mechanisms greased;the car really has that GM feeling,worn out bearings in the steering collumn,guages with the needles stuck pointing where they've never been before,sagging urethane nose,and of course,rattly doors.But I like it,and it's getting better by the day.
Z||000003||theogre||07-19-99||07:38 AM||||there is a kit in the red "help!" blister packs available from many parts dealers. There are 2 kits, with bushings & new pins, for GM. you want the shorter ones. You need on kit per hinge, and 2 kits are less than 10$us.
